        "original_id": "dfedb84c-3000-5240-965a-0da68bebcc97",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Clement Greenberg, Agatha Christie, Joseph Drapell, Jack Bush\n- Roles: art critic, essayist, novelist, short story writer, playwright, artist\n- Organizations: Cranbrook Academy\n- Topics: American Modern art\n\nFacts:\n- Agatha Christie was born on 15 September 1890 and died on 12 January 1976.\n- Agatha Christie, born Agatha Mary Clarissa Miller and later titled Dame Agatha Mary Clarissa Christie, Lady Mallowan, DBE, was an English crime novelist, short story writer, and playwright.\n- Clement Greenberg was born on January 16, 1909 and died on May 7, 1994.\n- Clement Greenberg sometimes wrote under the pseudonym K. Hardesh.\n- Clement Greenberg was an American essayist and an influential visual art critic closely associated with mid-20th-century American Modern art.\n- At the Cranbrook Academy, Joseph Drapell met visiting Canadian artist Jack Bush and American art critic Clement Greenberg.\n- Jack Bush and Clement Greenberg influenced Joseph Drapell's work.",
